KNOWNBUG: [class.inhctor.init] -- an inheriting constructor (`using Base::Base;`)
should make the base constructors usable for the derived class.  CBMC detects
the using-declaration but skips it (inheriting constructors are not
implemented), so the derived class is constructed by (mistaken) aggregate
initialisation and the constructor arguments (here a forwarded parameter pack)
are dropped, leaving the object default-initialised.  Flip to CORE once
inheriting constructors are supported.
